# Synapse-Network-Growing Cursor Rules

Read these first:

1. `AGENTS.md`
2. `ARCHITECTURE.md`
3. `docs/design-docs/system-design-principles.md`

For workflow, planning, scheduler, release, notification, runtime, auth, finance, settlement, or production-safety work, also read `.github/instructions/architecture-constraints.instructions.md`.

Do not duplicate architecture rules here. `ARCHITECTURE.md` is the shared source for Cursor, Codex, Copilot, Gemini, and Claude.

## Critical UI Rules

1. NEVER USE DRAWERS for new UI work. Do not add Drawer, Slide-out, Offcanvas, Side Panel, or right-side sheet components for create, edit, view, form, confirmation, or detail interactions.
2. ALWAYS USE CENTERED MODALS for popups, forms, confirmations, creation flows, and editing flows. The modal must be centered on screen.
3. Modal backgrounds must use a dark overlay mask that blocks interaction with the underlying page.
4. New Ops Console UI must follow the vendored `ui-ux-pro-max` SaaS / Ops Console design guidance from `.agents/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md`.
